From b7ecebb4a7da18772a8392052b955d983c5b3c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] redfin 1035: early swap retire on the GPU present path,
 kern.sweet_fb_early_retire (default 0)

r64u presents through the 0944 swap queue (sweetfbx 0x107, sweetfbflip=1, scanout off): CA learns a swap is done
from SwapWait polls, which answer 0 at once, and from type-5 ticks (sweetswapdone 1, off). CA's chain stays at 2
surfaces and the GPU idles ~6 ms/frame. Idea from UniXNU GopFramebuffer (sheng early retire): a swap is retired as
soon as its present blit is accepted onto the ring.

kern.sweet_fb_early_retire MASK, live:
  1  swap-complete tick at ring acceptance (swapDone where 4), no tick at the blit fence
  2  re-kick: a put-off queued present is retried at each vsync tick and when the previous blit's fence is seen
  4  SwapWait polls answer kIOReturnBusy while the swap is still queued / being presented, 0 once on the ring
Hazard: the blit reads CA's surface after retirement; CA's next GPU render into it is queued after the blit on the
same in-order ring (blit IB: CACHE_INVALIDATE + WFI first, CCU flush + CACHE_FLUSH_TS last), so it is safe for GPU
rendering; a CPU write by CA into a retired surface could tear (CA renders with metal2vulkan here). No copy-out.
Line: SWEET FB: early retire 5s: retired N | polls busy B done D stale S | rekick K | mode M.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC2ugyLE29nbFLJoQZd
